{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.QRatioBetaFactors","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QRatioBetaFactors","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SchurPrincipalBetaForm"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qratio_factor_upper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qratio_factor_upper","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QRatioBetaFactors.lean#L65-L84","doc":"**The `q`-ratio factor at a pair above `a`** (`j < a`, so `β_a < β_j`).\n\n`(Q·Q^{β_a} − Q^{β_j})/(Q^{β_a} − Q^{β_j}) = Q · (1 − Q^{β_j−β_a−1})/(1 − Q^{β_j−β_a})`\n\n— the same `P(β')`-over-`P(β)` factor, times **one** `Q`.  Summed over the `a` rows above, those\n`Q`s are the `Q^a` that `nPart_addCell` accounts for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qratio_factor_lower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qratio_factor_lower","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QRatioBetaFactors.lean#L44-L63","doc":"**The `q`-ratio factor at a pair below `a`** (`j > a`, so `β_j ≤ β_a`).\n\n`(Q·Q^{β_a} − Q^{β_j})/(Q^{β_a} − Q^{β_j}) = (1 − Q^{β_a+1−β_j})/(1 − Q^{β_a−β_j})`\n\n— the right-hand side is exactly the `P(β')`-factor over the `P(β)`-factor, with **no** leftover\npower of `Q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.betaR_addCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.betaR_addCell","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QRatioBetaFactors.lean#L36-L40","doc":"**Adding a box at row `a` raises exactly one β-number.** ","signatureChunk":0}]}